11. Complexity

Let $T_{\text{dev}}, T_{\text{test}}$ be template counts, $m$ variants per template, $K$ candidate pairs, $R_{\text{ref}} = 3$ reference runs per trial, $B = 1000$ bootstrap resamples, $K_c = 6$ loss classes, $|\mathcal{G}| = 27$ cost triples.

· Reference runs. Phase A: $T_{\text{dev}} m R_{\text{ref}}$. Phase C: $T_{\text{test}} m R_{\text{ref}}$. Phase A includes the paired-protocol experiment (50 templates $\times$ $m$ variants $\times$ $2$ extra runs).
· System runs. $K (T_{\text{dev}} + T_{\text{test}}) m$ verifications.
· Statistical estimation. CP bounds: $O(K |\mathcal{G}|)$ per estimate. Cluster bootstrap: $O(B T_{\text{test}} K |\mathcal{G}|)$ operations; with $B = 1000$, $T_{\text{test}} \le 300$, $K \le 6$, $|\mathcal{G}| = 27$, this is $\approx 5 \times 10^7$ operations — seconds on a laptop. Max-$t$ over classes: $O(B T_{\text{test}} K_c |\mathcal{G}|)$ additional, same order.
· Power simulation. $|\rho_{\text{grid}}| \cdot |\text{methods}| \cdot |T_{\text{grid}}| \cdot n_{\text{rep}} \approx 1.4 \times 10^5$ exact binomial-tail evaluations; minutes on a laptop.
· Storage. Records: $O(K (T_{\text{dev}} + T_{\text{test}}) m)$ triples; sealed labels: $O((T_{\text{dev}} + T_{\text{test}}) m)$; paired-protocol records: $O(50 \cdot m \cdot 2)$.
· Cost frontier. $O(|\mathcal{G}| \cdot \text{cost of one adoption decision})$; negligible relative to the trial cost.

The pipeline is dominated by reference re-execution. The revised version adds the three-run protocol (50% more reference runs than the earlier version) and the paired-protocol experiment (a small additional cost), but the statistical and cost-frontier analyses remain rounding errors. The additional reference runs are the price of a measured $\epsilon_{\text{ref}}$, and that price is the correct place to pay it.

